{"name":"Adventure Island Pink","hex":"#f87858","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adventure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feeling of desire for new and exciting things.","A remarkable occurrence; a striking event."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To risk oneself. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To risk oneself; to dare to go somewhere or undertake something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adventure"},{"term":"island","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, totally surrounded by water.","A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, partially surrounded by water; a peninsula; a half-island."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To surround with water; make into an island.","To set, dot (as if) with islands."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/island"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adventure","blocks":[{"text":"An adventure is a novel and exciting undertaking that is typically bold, sometimes risky. Adventures may be activities with danger such as traveling, exploring, skydiving, mountain climbing, scuba diving, river rafting, other extreme sports, or, importantly, any other activity that may be new, fresh or difficult and may even lead to failure. Adventure can take many forms beyond the typically described outdoor area. Adventures are often undertaken to create psychological arousal or in order to achieve a greater goal, such as the pursuit of knowledge that can only be obtained by such activities."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adventure","wikidata":"Q1436734"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island","wikidata":"Q23442"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg/500px-Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg/1280px-Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg/500px-Alice%27s_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lewis Carroll's Alice's Adventures in Wonderland is a well-known example of a fantasized adventure story.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlice's_Adventures_in_Wonderland_-_Carroll%2C_Robinson_-_S001_-_Cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg/500px-Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg/1280px-Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg/500px-Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Galapagos penguin is endemic to the Galápagos Islands.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_(Spheniscus_mendiculus)_male.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Pteropus_seychellensis.jpg/500px-Pteropus_seychellensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Pteropus_seychellensis.jpg/500px-Pteropus_seychellensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Seychelles fruit bat has a major role in distributing the seeds of trees between islands, a form of oceanic dispersal.[24]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APteropus_seychellensis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Finchadaptiveradiation.png/500px-Finchadaptiveradiation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Finchadaptiveradiation.png/500px-Finchadaptiveradiation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adaptive radiation of finch A (Geospiza magnirostris) into three other species of finches on the Galapagos Islands. Due to the absence of other birds, Darwin's finches adapted to new niches. Their seed-eating beaks evolved to handle foods such as nuts, fruits, and insects.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFinchadaptiveradiation.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg/500px-Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg/1280px-Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg/500px-Dronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The extinct Dodo is an example of island gigantism.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADronte_dodo_Raphus_cucullatus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Breadfruit_%28Artocarpus_altilis%29%2C_Malaysia.JPG/500px-Breadfruit_%28Artocarpus_altilis%29%2C_Malaysia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons